Note: Phase 36 IMPROV-01 — baseline #classical rule pack
Note: Loaded at FlowEngine init by StyleRegistry.LoadAtEngineInit
Note: See flow-lang/improv/styles/README.md for the Dict shape contract.
Note:
Note: Classical character: tight chord-tone weight on strong beats (the
Note: harmonic skeleton stays explicit), scale-tone-favored on weak beats with
Note: ZERO chromatic_passing (classical purity), step-down/step-up dominate
Note: intervals (smooth voice leading), legato/tenuto articulations for the
Note: long-line phrasing.

use "@improv"

(registerStyle #classical
    (dict
        Note: ---- Beat-strength weights — explicit harmony, no chromatic ----
        #beat_weights (dict
            #strong (dict #chord_tone 0.85 #scale_tone 0.15 #chromatic_passing 0.00)
            #weak   (dict #chord_tone 0.40 #scale_tone 0.60 #chromatic_passing 0.00))

        Note: ---- Interval transitions — smooth voice leading ----
        Note: stepwise heavily preferred; chromatic minimized; small leaps allowed.
        #interval_transitions (dict
            #step_up 0.38 #step_down 0.38
            #leap_up 0.08 #leap_down 0.10
            #chromatic 0.02 #repeat 0.04)

        Note: ---- Rhythmic template — eighth-note straight feel ----
        #rhythmic_template <<#eighth #eighth #eighth #eighth #eighth #eighth #eighth #eighth>>

        Note: ---- Articulation distribution — long-line phrasing ----
        #articulation_distribution (dict
            #downbeat   #legato
            #offbeat    #tenuto
            #syncopated #legato)))
